Completes patch 0005, which disabled the WPA3/SAE defaults under HWSIM_RADIO
for the *AP-side* VAPs (cfg.u.bss_info.security, two sites) but missed the
*STA-side* equivalent (cfg.u.sta_info.security) in the isVapSTAMesh() branch
of the same file. The result was a security mismatch between the two ends of
the EasyMesh backhaul link:

  - controller's mesh_backhaul_5g AP (bss_info, patched by 0005): WPA2-PSK,
    MFP disabled, AES-CCMP
  - extender's mesh_sta_5g STA (sta_info, NOT patched):           WPA3-SAE,
    MFP *required*, key type SAE

Root-caused by following the connection attempt all the way down after the
SSID fix (rdk-wifi-hal 0009) got the extender to actually start connecting:

  1. Extender's state machine now finds the candidate and calls
     wifi_hal_connect(vap 15, bssid 02:00:00:e1:16:33) every cycle --
     confirmed via ext_try_connecting:1175 "connecting to ssid:mesh_backhaul".
  2. nl80211_connect_sta() runs to completion ("Proceeding with legacy Auth")
     and calls sme_send_authentication().
  3. But wifi_supplicant_drv_authenticate() -- the driver op that actually
     builds NL80211_CMD_AUTHENTICATE -- is NEVER reached: its "Enter" debug
     print never appears in /tmp/wifiHal, and `iw event` shows zero auth/assoc
     frames over many full connect cycles (only scan started/finished).
  4. sme_send_authentication() (wpa_supplicant/sme.c) returns void and bails
     silently via wpas_connect_work_done() when wpa_supplicant_set_suites()
     fails -- which is exactly what a key-mgmt/cipher/MFP mismatch between the
     STA's configured suites and the AP's advertised RSN IE produces. It logs
     only at MSG_WARNING through wpa_msg(), which is not routed anywhere in
     this build, hence the complete silence.

The non-BananaPi branch immediately below already contains exactly the right
values for this case (wpa2_personal / mfp_disabled / aes), so gate the
BananaPi-R4 WPA3 block behind !HWSIM_RADIO and fall through to it -- the same
one-line change, and the same rationale, as 0005 applied to the AP side. Real
BananaPi R4 hardware is unaffected.

---
 source/db/wifi_db.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/db/wifi_db.c b/source/db/wifi_db.c
--- a/source/db/wifi_db.c
+++ b/source/db/wifi_db.c
@@ -371,7 +371,7 @@
             cfg.u.sta_info.security.encr = wifi_encryption_aes;
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
         } else {
-#if defined(_PLATFORM_BANANAPI_R4_)
+#if defined(_PLATFORM_BANANAPI_R4_) && !defined(HWSIM_RADIO)
             cfg.u.sta_info.security.mode = wifi_security_mode_wpa3_personal;
             cfg.u.sta_info.security.wpa3_transition_disable = false;
             cfg.u.sta_info.security.mfp = wifi_mfp_cfg_required;
@@ -385,7 +385,7 @@
             cfg.u.sta_info.security.mfp = wifi_mfp_cfg_disabled;
             cfg.u.sta_info.security.mode = wifi_security_mode_wpa2_personal;
             cfg.u.sta_info.security.encr = wifi_encryption_aes;
-#endif // _PLATFORM_BANANAPI_R4_
+#endif // _PLATFORM_BANANAPI_R4_ && !HWSIM_RADIO
         }
         cfg.u.sta_info.enabled = false;
         cfg.u.sta_info.scan_params.period = 10;
